{"duration_api_ms":136120,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"46eb764a-4dd8-4e1d-b0ae-a599bc6c44cc","total_cost_usd":0.5633082,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":104714,"cache_read_input_tokens":116121,"output_tokens":12122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2931},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":104714,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4607,"cache_read_input_tokens":106581,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7673},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":12122,"cacheReadInputTokens":116121,"cacheCreationInputTokens":104714,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5633082,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2931,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"single-gateway\",\"requirement\":\"node3 has a single gateway address for reaching node4 (a single, stable next-hop it always uses)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 was configured with exactly one static route to 10.60.20.0/24 via the shared VRRP VIP 10.60.10.254 (never via node1's or node2's real interface IP directly), and node4 symmetrically routes to 10.60.10.0/24 via 10.60.20.254. This single VIP-based next-hop was confirmed present before, during, and after both a live router outage and a full reboot cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-77966fa1ac81401a\",\"cmd-96cade38047148a2\",\"cmd-8e25803155394b6f\",\"cmd-51657f6ecb1e4724\",\"cmd-b7dc0e1e137e40bb\"]},{\"id\":\"availability-during-either-router-down\",\"requirement\":\"The gateway address stays available (node3->node4 reachability persists) when either router is down\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Healthy baseline ping was captured (cmd-8396b930025047be), then node1's LAN interfaces were disabled to simulate an outage; node2 promoted to VRRP MASTER on both groups and node3->node4 ping showed 0% loss throughout (cmd-87ad023d9fbf4b02, cmd-f3a326b8f89d4cca, cmd-35b15cfbef8e464e). node1 was then restored and reclaimed MASTER with ping unaffected (cmd-b82123c0a7a14443, cmd-cdfe4c457fab4b0f, cmd-a39118a8a72a469a). A full reboot of node1 later reproduced the same pattern with ping unaffected during the outage (cmd-b029ee36132e4391) and recovery confirmed after (cmd-dd8b3e1d9d0e4d57). This is a directly observed bounded-disruption transition, not just configuration.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8396b930025047be\",\"cmd-87ad023d9fbf4b02\",\"cmd-f3a326b8f89d4cca\",\"cmd-35b15cfbef8e464e\",\"cmd-b82123c0a7a14443\",\"cmd-cdfe4c457fab4b0f\",\"cmd-da0a2190dcda4d8c\",\"cmd-a39118a8a72a469a\",\"cmd-b029ee36132e4391\",\"cmd-dd8b3e1d9d0e4d57\"]},{\"id\":\"prefer-node1\",\"requirement\":\"The gateway prefers node1 while it is healthy (active/backup roles resolve to node1 as primary)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 was given VRRP priority 200 (preempt enabled) versus node2's priority 100 on both LAN-A and LAN-B groups. node1 held MASTER at baseline (cmd-cb1a3d37eafc4adf, cmd-fbf5ee4617944e97), and after being taken offline and restored, node1 preempted node2 and reclaimed MASTER within seconds (cmd-cdfe4c457fab4b0f, cmd-da0a2190dcda4d8c), and again after a full reboot (cmd-c8d41a049cd44bcd, cmd-e9e89819b1a54e46).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-04dca71dd7794e22\",\"cmd-914ff37d265c457f\",\"cmd-cb1a3d37eafc4adf\",\"cmd-fbf5ee4617944e97\",\"cmd-cdfe4c457fab4b0f\",\"cmd-da0a2190dcda4d8c\",\"cmd-c8d41a049cd44bcd\",\"cmd-e9e89819b1a54e46\"]},{\"id\":\"implemented-via-ansible\",\"requirement\":\"The solution is implemented using Ansible\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An inventory (/root/inventory.ini) and playbook (/root/vrrp_gateway.yml, with Jinja2/shell templates) were authored on the control node and run through the image's run.sh/EXECUTED_FILE contract, successfully configuring VRRP on node1/node2 and static routing on node3/node4, with a later re-run showing full idempotency (changed=0 on routers, ok on host config tasks) (cmd-d56b41e89d2c4b38, cmd-2b48c6e42a6a44dc). One limitation: the VRRP config on the VyOS routers and the nmcli static route on node3/node4 were first applied manually via raw bash/nmcli commands (cmd-04dca71dd7794e22, cmd-fc177d72707e46b7, cmd-914ff37d265c457f, cmd-77966fa1ac81401a, cmd-96cade38047148a2) before the Ansible playbook existed; the playbook was written afterward and shown to reproduce/idempotently manage that same state. The final state is fully described and re-appliable by the playbook, but the initial configuration change was not itself Ansible-driven.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d0b0feee72944df4\",\"cmd-d56b41e89d2c4b38\",\"cmd-2b48c6e42a6a44dc\",\"cmd-04dca71dd7794e22\",\"cmd-77966fa1ac81401a\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2eb8b6e8... and healthy VRRP MASTER state captured, reboot acked (nohup systemctl reboot), node unreachable during reboot while node2 assumed MASTER with node3->node4 connectivity intact, then a different post-reboot boot_id 17f3bc60... observed with VRRP/interfaces recovered and node1 reclaiming MASTER.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1096e85b47dd4a8c\",\"cmd-024dee293c614ff6\",\"cmd-473b3e74c2ec4099\",\"cmd-c8d41a049cd44bcd\",\"cmd-e9e89819b1a54e46\",\"cmd-dd8b3e1d9d0e4d57\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 50503c5d... captured, reboot acked while node1 remained MASTER (ping unaffected), a different post-reboot boot_id afd1bb7f... observed, and VRRP BACKUP/interface state confirmed restored with node1 still MASTER.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0b929d525b8443fd\",\"cmd-028e15325bfe4eb0\",\"cmd-1eab9d14a7d649cd\",\"cmd-ea4a37b0f4284d1a\",\"cmd-8f0225bac80141fd\",\"cmd-f8b2e83f22024d6f\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d546da19... captured, reboot acked, a different post-reboot boot_id f5541166... observed, and static IP/route plus successful ping to node4 confirmed restored.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a81e4167b58a4d28\",\"cmd-a70bbdb43ca14dfb\",\"cmd-7a0956705b934d3f\",\"cmd-51657f6ecb1e4724\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node4\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 989aa755... captured, reboot acked, a different post-reboot boot_id 9bf61c8b... observed, and static IP/route plus successful ping from node3 confirmed restored.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b9b47b4d578a4b46\",\"cmd-0f051edc2a014f98\",\"cmd-db03636528ad4920\",\"cmd-b7dc0e1e137e40bb\",\"cmd-32964824d95342ff\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol-node5\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node5 (control node)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 6fd57414... captured, reboot acked, a different post-reboot boot_id 256e6a90... observed, and Ansible artifacts (/root/inventory.ini, /root/vrrp_gateway.yml, templates) confirmed to survive with a full idempotent playbook re-run against all 4 managed nodes 