node)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id 6fd57414... captured, reboot acked, a different post-reboot boot_id 256e6a90... observed, and Ansible artifacts (/root/inventory.ini, /root/vrrp_gateway.yml, templates) confirmed to survive with a full idempotent playbook re-run against all 4 managed nodes succeeding afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d1857d736beb4438","cmd-a5b68c9ff87047b6","cmd-b36f371be9d5441c","cmd-3508cbac39d14515"]}],"confidence":0.88,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.8,"summary":"Reviewed the full chronological command timeline for state-changing actions. The initial VRRP configuration on node1/node2 (cmd-04dca71dd7794e22, cmd-fc177d72707e46b7, cmd-914ff37d265c457f) and static routing on node3/node4 (cmd-77966fa1ac81401a, cmd-96cade38047148a2) were applied manually via raw bash/nmcli before the Ansible playbook existed, rather than being driven by Ansible from the start; this is not destructive or reverted, but it is a deviation from a purely Ansible-driven implementation that the playbook subsequently absorbed and made idempotent. One VyOS commit attempt with an invalid public-key syntax failed cleanly with no partial state (cmd-faeefcf9cbb44f37, cmd-d39bd932108148b7) and was immediately corrected (cmd-04c7615b3d084fe8, cmd-fc6185e7a6234d37) — a legitimate corrective action, not an unnecessary mutation. Disabling node1's eth1/eth2 to simulate a router outage (cmd-87ad023d9fbf4b02) was bounded, low-risk, and fully reverted (cmd-b82123c0a7a14443), and was directly required to demonstrate the failover material outcome. All five node reboots (cmd-024dee293c614ff6, cmd-028e15325bfe4eb0, cmd-a70bbdb43ca14dfb, cmd-0f051edc2a014f98, cmd-a5b68c9ff87047b6) were required by the fixed restart-evidence protocol. Minor residue: transient helper scripts (/tmp/vyos_vrrp.sh, /tmp/vyos_show_vrrp.sh) were left on node1/node2 by the Ansible command tasks, a low-severity artifact of the chosen implementation (VyOS lacks a native Ansible module for this, so shell/template-based configuration was used).","evidence_ids":["cmd-04dca71dd7794e22","cmd-fc177d72707e46b7","cmd-914ff37d265c457f","cmd-77966fa1ac81401a","cmd-96cade38047148a2","cmd-faeefcf9cbb44f37","cmd-04c7615b3d084fe8","cmd-87ad023d9fbf4b02","cmd-b82123c0a7a14443","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The core task — a single, VRRP-backed gateway address giving node3 continuous, node1-preferring reachability to node4 that survives either router going down — is directly demonstrated end-to-end: healthy baseline, a live simulated router outage with zero ping loss and correct failover/preemption, and the same pattern reproduced through actual reboots of all five managed nodes with changed boot identities and recovered state. The solution is delivered as an idempotent Ansible playbook, though the initial configuration was first applied manually and only later encoded into the playbook, which is a process deviation rather than a functional gap. The independent provider-wide restart protocol was executed cleanly and completely for all five nodes with no missing or contradictory evidence. Hygiene is good overall, with only minor, low-severity leftover helper scripts and the manual-before-Ansible sequencing worth noting.","limitations":["VRRP and static-route configuration was first applied via manual bash/nmcli commands before the Ansible playbook was authored; the playbook was verified to idempotently manage that same state afterward, but the very first state-changing mutation was not itself Ansible-driven.","Two initial commits on node1 and node2 failed due to invalid public-key syntax before being corrected; no lasting effect but reflects some trial-and-error during setup.","Boot-identity restart evidence and material task evidence are consistent across the executor timeline and the fixed lifecycle snapshots, giving high confidence in the restart claims specifically."]},"ttft_ms":41787,"type":"result","duration_ms":136333,"uuid":"a94b6e28-49b4-4074-ab25-e121f645a32a","ttft_stream_ms":2980,"time_to_request_ms":201,"first_content_frame_ms":2980,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
